{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1087667-pledges-consequence-and-you","id":1087667,"title":"Pledges, Consequence, and You!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-04T07:25:58-07:00","id":1087667,"title":"Pledges, Consequence, and You!","content":"Howdy y'all! So, I've been trying to get myself back into the RP swing of things as of late. Changeling is by far my favorite setting. In part because it gives the player some explicit reigns for steering their own story (the brightest, I think, being the +1 - +3 dice that can be added to Dream Combat just for being really entertaining about it xD)<br /> <br /> Still, I think that pledges are always tricky because it becomes a mechanical benefit with only as much consequence as an ST wants to make about it. I'm curious how other people handle that. I think about them as a way of fielding what you'd like to see happen with the story. 1e's Freehold Blessings did this pretty well, I think. Subtlety means you should be rolling to conceal your nature constantly in the setting. Fortitude is seeing a lot of terrible things -- Fertility for making a lot of crazy things happen with Glamour.<br /> <br /> But some of the issues of actual consequence seems, to me, particularly true with Freehold pledges. The Freehold represents the community the players' characters are a part of. Which means that the only way to bring in the interesting elements of a consequence is from an ST forcing it or needing the player to actively muck something up that is otherwise a right of entry into any story that includes characters being part of one.<br /> <br /> The 2e changes seem to be trying to address this with the idea of Stories and Approaches, particularly with the Huntsmen as central antagonist, but it still doesn't bring up much of what the player character is risking by making a bunch of long term pledges that never really put them at risk beyond a flavorful (I get more punchies because I make shoes for this one guy down the block, you all saw it!) hook. I like the idea of Sealing as a short term way of engaging with that but even it mentions the issue of &quot;Let's all pledge to get each other burgers and get some mechanical bonus for it&quot; business<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a topic that always boils down to ST discretion but I thought it would make for a neat conversation, hear about how other people have handled pledges, things that did or didn't work, just -- ya know, chatter I suppose ^-^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13346-piggysayswhat","name":"PiggySaysWhat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:43:32-07:00","id":1087680,"title":"","content":"Approaches aren't a thing anymore, it's now Bargains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:48:33-07:00","id":1087764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1087667-pledges-consequence-and-you?p=1087680#post1087680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Approaches aren't a thing anymore, it's now Bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Groovy, however Hunstmen protocols will ultimately be handled works for me. I liked the idea of them needing to, or at least being incentivised mechanically, to deal with players on the terms they set out with their character. I think it's always nice when an ST does that but seeing it worked into the mechanics seems smart. Particularly when delving into the possibilities of rotating ST duties addressed in the Chronicles core.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm curious about how people handle the idea of giving Pledges weight generally. I guess it's that I always view mechanics as a means of developing risk (which is the core ingredient for enforcing the tenant of a &quot;good&quot; story with drama.)<br /> <br /> Lots of pledges don't seem to involve much punch for that, just reward for already agreeing to play by the terms of what they were going to do anyway. Does it always boil down to just ST discretion, or have people tried their own flavorful workarounds? When did they work out well, when did they fall a little flat? That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Obviously I'm speaking in abstracts, which is rough, but Pledges between ST characters is just coloring an STs power to add +/- consequence to things ... which seems generally assumed as an ability to me. Between characters, unless they're part of a broad plot, they seem to only have a RP risk. You either choose to break it or don't.<br /> <br /> I guess a kind of extended action roll could be a way to address it, requiring a Changeling to meet a certain threshold with side pledges or else be hit by the failure to uphold but again, I'm just kind of curious about other people's thoughts and how they've handled it/seen it handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13346-piggysayswhat","name":"PiggySaysWhat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:01:12-07:00","id":1087836,"title":"","content":"For Changeling 2e it's impossible really know how to answer that until we know what Rose and Meghan have planned for how Pledges work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:36:04-07:00","id":1087861,"title":"","content":"I suppose, though it wasn't like this wasn't an issue with 1e. I think it's also a question with any policy of debt and payment (Boons, and the like.) I'm not so much looking for a rules answer, particularly as everything is getting hashed out from an official standpoint. I'm also not sure that there ever can be an official way of making it a hard line ruling. The question of time and whether or not any given player can be there for the game their characters make a pledge in will fluctuate in any given chronicle.<br /> <br /> I'm more curious about people's actual experience in trying to work through them -- assuming they view it as an issue at all. Was there a time when making a Pledge, as a Changeling, felt important and charged with consequence -- or does it always work out as a way to bandaid mechanical effects until they are made &quot;official&quot; with exp?<br /> <br /> I have never been a part of a game in which a player to player Pledge was ever able to make its full arc of either success or failure, it always just sat as a mechanical effect that <i>could </i>be taken advantage of but never seemed to be. Sealing seems like a way to encourage micro level engagement, but the macro extending beyond a week or a month still seems to get hazy.<br /> <br /> If it's a dead duck of a question until 2e is finalized, that's alright. Just trying to get a gauge of things as I try to think about ways to handle something that is always pushed so hard as a fundamental of Changeling life that I don't always see blossom out of the Deus Ex Machina realm of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13346-piggysayswhat","name":"PiggySaysWhat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T17:00:55-07:00","id":1088000,"title":"","content":"Okay I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:54:02-07:00","id":1088069,"title":"","content":"1e had some serious mechanical issues that were very easy to abuse, and I ended up homebrewing new ones. (Basically I removed duration and made boon equal to the lesser of task or sanction)<br /> <br /> In terms of RP I did have one character who used pledges to great effect. Whenever he needed to persuade someone to trust him he would respond with &quot;I swear on my True Name to tell you no lies this day&quot; which tended to intimidate people into listening to whatever he had to say. For most people the inability to tell a lie paired with the devastating penalties for violating a True Name Oath would be a hugely uncomfortable and frightening lose lose situation with no real upside, but he was an elemental with no dots in subterfuge. It made everybody uncomfortable that he would voluntarily self inflict that kind of handicap just to make a point, but giving up a skill he didn't have in the first place was well worth the benefit of being unquestionably trusted at his word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T11:13:42-07:00","id":1088803,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that sounds smart for getting rid of duration. It always did seem like the easiest way for bouncing the pledge-check to a point where there was no real risk for what was gained. Hopefully the tying in of Beats as the way to get xp will make those choices seem less efficient. Sure, a toon can get all the special dice/perks, but is losing out on the Beats if they don't start using them to put themselves at risk.<br /> <br /> That is a really neat use of Pledge fear, which doesn't seem to get brought up much in the more common toothless situations. Basically, turning the True Tongue flaw into a social merit , but in a really fitting way for an elemental. It does still seem dependent on an antagonist NPC/PC to have a grudge and force him to choose between trying to lie or facing some other dire consequence to make it a real issue for that character. Sounds like the RP opportunities to get people questioning Pledge bluffs would be worth it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13346-piggysayswhat","name":"PiggySaysWhat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:11:40-07:00","id":1089527,"title":"","content":"Honesty Pledges are also extremely effective in an interrogation context. Terrifying somebody into talking doesn't normally work because they just tell you what they think you want to hear, but if you intimidate them into agreeing to a Pledge to tell the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth you can ensure the information is accurate to the best of their knowledge.<br /> <br /> (We did this to my Fetch to find out to what extent he was working with a hobgoblin slaver. The best part was that the only consequence was a minor pishogue. &quot;Nothing much happens if you lie, but we'll know.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T19:45:33-07:00","id":1090563,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah -- that's a cool use of them. The bane quality sounds like it would maintain some weight whether short or long-term. Avoiding something crucial/helpful seems like the best way to make things feel risky. Even with with most Freehold pledges being basically just &quot;don't help loyalists&quot; even if that seems implied in a pure protagonist vs. antagonist game.<br /> <br /> It makes me think that perhaps the best way to deal with &quot;meh&quot; pledges is to find a way to tie them into short-term risk, even if they're long-term. So, something like a character having to choose between telling lies under Pledge-oath <i>or</i> end up helping the loyalists would make it feel like a part of play, rather than just hanging out in the background.<br /> <br /> Thanks for sharing sharing some of the ways Pledges worked out/got used in your games, they've gotten my noggin' revving and it's much appreciated ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13346-piggysayswhat","name":"PiggySaysWhat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}